<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    The two checks this project disagrees with, and why. Everything else lint
    reports as an error is a real one and fails the build - see the lint block
    in build.gradle.

    Kept as a file rather than as suppressions at each site: both of these are
    decisions about the whole app, made once and written down in CLAUDE.md,
    and scattering them across two hundred plural entries would say the
    opposite - that each was judged on its own.
-->
<lint>

    <!--
        Which plural forms a language has is the language's business.

        Russian and Polish need "few" and "many"; English has only "one" and
        "other". Lint reads every language's set against a table of what CLDR
        says that language *can* take and calls a missing one an error, which
        turns a correct Czech translation into twelve build failures.

        What actually matters here is enforced by scripts/check-strings.py,
        which is stricter where it counts and quiet where it does not: every
        form must take the same arguments as English, "other" must exist, and
        a name must be a plural in every language or in none. See CLAUDE.md,
        "A new string is nine files".
    -->
    <issue id="MissingQuantity" severity="ignore" />

    <!--
        Predictive back is handled, in both of the ways it has to be.

        targetSdk 36 turns predictive back on by default, so from API 33 an
        OnBackInvokedCallback is registered and the key never arrives; below
        33 there is no dispatcher at all and onKeyDown/onBackPressed remains
        the path, because minSdk is 30. Lint sees the second half and reports
        the first as missing. Both are deliberate and exclusive - see
        EmulatorActivity.registerBackCallback and CLAUDE.md on targetSdk.
    -->
    <issue id="GestureBackNavigation" severity="ignore" />

</lint>
